5 Real-Life Applications of Linear Search

📱 Finding a Contact
When you search through a small contact list, the system can check names one by one until it finds the person you're looking for.

📚 Searching for a Book
Imagine checking books on a shelf from left to right until you find “Introduction to Python.” That's essentially linear search in action.

🛒 Finding an Item in a Shopping List
If you have a list like ["Milk", "Bread", "Rice", "Apples"] and want to find "Rice", you can check each item sequentially.

🎓 Finding a Student's Record
In a small classroom record, the system can examine each student's name one by one until it finds the required student.
